## 1. What MotionAI is: the mental model

MotionAI is a Flutter app (Windows desktop + Android phone) with a pure-Dart engine. Think of it as
After Effects with a JSON command API:

```
Project
 ├─ media[]          imported files (image / video / audio) → media ids "m_…"
 ├─ main             the main Composition (what export renders)
 ├─ comps{}          nested compositions (precomps, shots)  → comp ids
 ├─ recipes / shots  saved camera moves, saved layer recipes, add_shot shots
 └─ Composition
      ├─ width, height, fps, duration, background, motion_blur, dof
      ├─ camera      2D or 3D camera (one-node / two-node, lens, DOF, keyframes)
      └─ layers[]    layers[0] is the TOP layer
           Layer: id, name, type (video|image|text|solid|null|audio|shape|comp),
                  start, duration (end = start + duration), source_in, speed,
                  is3d, visible, locked, parent, matte, path, blend,
                  transform props: position [x,y,z], anchor [x,y,z], scale [%x,%y,%z],
                                   rotation [x,y,z °], opacity 0-100, volume 0-200,
                  effects[] (each with animatable params), masks[], text style, shape, geo spec
```

- **Units.** Time in **seconds** (composition time). Positions in **composition pixels**: x right,
  y down, z away from the viewer; (0,0) = top-left; frame centre = (width/2, height/2). Scale in
  percent. Rotation in degrees. Colours `"#RRGGBB"` (alpha `"#RRGGBBAA"` for transparent solids).
- **Animatable properties.** Every transform prop and every effect / mask parameter is an `AnimProp`:
  either a static value or a list of keyframes with an ease each. An ease controls motion **from that
  keyframe to the next** (`linear, hold, ease_in, ease_out, easy_ease, bounce, elastic, back`).
- **2D vs 3D.** A 2D camera (pan / zoom / rotate / shake) affects every layer. The 3D camera only
  affects layers with `is3d: true`; 2D layers stay flat on screen (good for text / UI on top of a 3D
  scene). With `make_3d` the first frame looks identical and depth appears when the camera moves.
- **Parenting.** A child's transform is relative to its parent (like AE). Null layers are invisible
  handles: components are built as a null `<id>_g` with children `<id>_<part>`.
- **Precomps.** A `comp` layer shows another composition (with time remap / loop). `in_comp: <id>`
  runs any command inside that comp. `open_comp` switches what the editor shows. Shots made by
  `add_shot` are precomps with their own 3D camera.
- **Rendering.** The live editor preview and the export renderer share the engine. `render_frame` /
  `preview_shot` use the export renderer (offscreen); `editor_screenshot` is exactly what Mohit sees.
- **Undo.** Every `run_commands` batch, template insert, Director run and caption run is one undo step
  (`undo` / `redo` tools or Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y).
- **Autosave.** The project autosaves after edits; `save_project` forces it.

