## 6. Precomps (nested compositions) and bulk operations

### 6.1 Precomps

- `precompose {layers: [ids], name?, id? (new comp id), layer_id? (new comp layer id), move_attributes?:
  true}` — moves the layers into a new comp and puts ONE comp layer in their place (picture identical).
  Effects / masks / curve / glass_frame / 3D on the comp layer then apply to the whole group.
  `move_attributes: false` (one layer) keeps its transform / effects on the comp layer.
- `unprecompose {layer, keep_comp?, force?}`.
- `add_comp {id?, name, width?, height?, duration?, fps?, background?}` — new empty comp; fill it with
  `in_comp`.
- `add_layer {type: "comp", comp, start?, duration?, source_in?, loop?: true}` — reuse a comp any number of
  times. Time remap: `update_layer {layer, source_in, speed (0.05–16), loop}`.
- `open_comp {comp | "main"}` switches what later commands edit (CURRENT PROJECT shows `editing_comp`).
  A comp cannot contain itself.
- Building pattern for long videos: **one precomp per scene** (`S01`, `S02`, …) placed on main back to
  back, transitions between the comp layers on main. Edit inside with `in_comp`, look with
  `preview_shot {comp}`.

### 6.2 Bulk operations

- `for_layers {layers: [ids] | "selection", filter?: {type?: "text" | ["image","video"], name_contains?,
  is3d?, in_range?: [t0, t1], visible?, locked?, has_effect?, parent?}, command: {…single-layer op with
  "$layer"…} | commands: [...], skip_errors?: true}` — `$layer` → id (also inside strings, e.g.
  `"new_id": "$layer_b"`), `$index` → 0,1,2…, `$layer_start` / `$layer_end` → its times.
  E.g. fade in every text: `{"op":"for_layers","filter":{"type":"text"},"command":{"op":"animate_in",
  "layer":"$layer","preset":"fade"}}`.
- `select {layers | filter, mode?}` (also the `select` tool).
- `align {layers, mode: left|center|right|top|middle|bottom, to?: selection|comp|<layer id>}` ·
  `distribute {layers, axis: horizontal|vertical, by?: center|gap}`.
- `align_time {layers, mode: start|end|stagger|sequence, time?, step? | frames?, gap?, order?:
  given|stack|time}` · `shift_time {layers, by}`.
- `transform_layers {layers, move?: [dx, dy], scale? (factor), rotate? (deg), center?: [x, y]}`.
- `offset_property {layer, prop, by? | factor?}` (value and every keyframe).
- `parent_layers {layers, parent: id | null}` (keeps them in place) · `group_layers {layers, name?}`
  (null parent at their centre).
- `paste_layers {layers: [layer JSON], media?, comps?, time?, index?}` · `paste_effects {layer, effects,
  replace?}` · `paste_animation {layer, props, from_start?}` (the editor's copy / paste formats).

## 7. Components

`add_component {type, id?, start?, duration?, x?, y?, scale?, enter?, exit?, sfx?, …fields}`.
`x`, `y`, `size`, `width`, `height`, `*_size` accept a **fraction 0–1 of the frame** or pixels.
Every component is a group: null layer **`<id>_g`** with children **`<id>_<part>`** — move / scale /
fade / parent the group to move everything; `get_layers` shows the parts. One `add_component` = one
undo step. Sounds (pop / tick / paper / ui_click…) are added automatically unless `sfx: false`.
Full list of types: Appendix A.2 (76). `list_components` gives the live list.

