## 8. Maps and geo layers

Two systems exist. **Use the geo layer (8.1) for new work**: it re-projects every frame (GEOlayers
style), so camera flights stay sharp at any zoom. The older map components (8.2) are image-based kits
that still work and power some templates / patterns. **India is always drawn with India's official
boundary** in both.

### 8.1 Geo layers (win-40)

`add_geo {id?, style?, projection?, focus? | center? [lon, lat], zoom? (1 = whole world / whole globe),
highlight?, routes?, pins?, graticule?, borders?, labels?, texture?, font?, label_size?, border_width?,
dim_others?, atmosphere?, is3d?, reveal?: {start, duration}, fly?: {to, zoom?, start, duration}, start?,
duration?}` — a shape layer with a `geo` field.

- **Styles (12):** `dark_political` (Dark Political), `satellite` (Satellite Relief), `paper_vintage`,
  `blueprint`, `neon` (Neon Night), `clean_light` (Clean Light — the 2025 reference "light-grey map with
  saturated fills"), `newsprint` (Newsprint Ink), `documentary_gold`, `night_lights` (Night Lights — dark
  north Korea at night), `hologram` (Hologram HUD), `clay` (Clay 3D), `military` (Military Ops). Aliases:
  dark, political, sat, relief, paper, vintage, light, ink, gold, night, hud, ops.
- **Projections:** `equirectangular`, `mercator`, `natural_earth`, `globe` (with `atmosphere` rim).
- **focus:** a country name / ISO code → centre + fitting zoom. `center: [lon, lat]` + `zoom` for exact
  framing (lon first!).
- **highlight:** a country, or a list `[{code, fill?, stroke?, glow?: 0-100, extrude?: px (3D slab),
  label?: text | true, flag?: true, from?, to? (reveal window 0..1 of geo_progress)}]`.
- **routes:** `[{points: [[lon,lat], …] (great-circle legs), color, width, dashed, glow, arrow, arc?: 0..1
  (flight lift), comet?, from, to, label}]`.
- **pins:** `[{lon, lat, label, color, kind: dot|ring|pulse|diamond, at: 0..1, size}]`.
- `dim_others` darkens everything but the highlights; `labels` country names; `graticule` grid lines;
  `borders`, `border_width`, `font`, `label_size`; `texture` for satellite styles.
- `is3d: true` → pitch it with rotation X + the 3D camera (map tilts back in perspective).
- **Animate:** `set_keyframe` on `geo_center` [lon, lat], `geo_zoom` [x], `geo_progress` [0..100]
  (draws routes, reveals highlights / pins / labels in order, by their from / to / at windows).
  `reveal {start, duration}` keys geo_progress 0 → 100 for you.
- `update_geo {layer, …any add_geo key}` · `geo_fly {layer, to: country | [lon, lat], zoom?, from?,
  from_zoom?, start?, duration? (2.5), ease?, arc?: true (pull back mid-flight on long hops)}`.

Example — Korea fly-in, NK highlighted teal with a slab, pin, labels:
```json
[{"op":"add_geo","id":"map","style":"clean_light","projection":"mercator","center":[100,30],"zoom":1.4,
  "highlight":[{"code":"PRK","fill":"#3F8C86","extrude":18,"glow":30,"label":"NORTH KOREA","from":0.25,"to":0.45}],
  "pins":[{"lon":125.75,"lat":39.03,"kind":"pulse","color":"#E0201B","at":0.6}],
  "dim_others":true,"start":0,"duration":6},
 {"op":"geo_fly","layer":"map","to":"PRK","zoom":7,"start":0.3,"duration":3.2,"ease":"easy_ease"},
 {"op":"set_keyframe","target":"map","prop":"geo_progress","time":0.5,"value":[0]},
 {"op":"set_keyframe","target":"map","prop":"geo_progress","time":4.0,"value":[100]}]
```
Huge 3D country names (2025 reference look): a text layer (Anton / Bebas, `extrude: 30`, is3d) above the
map, or the highlight `label`. Ghost word behind: `map_watermark` (8.2).

### 8.2 Map components and map grammar (V3-A)

- `map {countries: [name | ISO | {code, fill?, label?: text|false, at? (s when named), label_rotate?}],
  focus?, bounds?: [[lat, lon], [lat, lon]] (also flat list or {north, south, east, west}), zoom?, style:
  dark|paper|blue|road|satellite, clouds?: true, fill_opacity? (0.62), stroke_width? (1.6), label_size?
  (0.06), label_opacity?, label_rotate?: "auto" | deg | 0, label_animator?: pop|typewriter|fade_up,
  label_stagger? (0.6), focus_dim? (60), cities?: [{name, lat, lon, at?, side?}], tilt? (+ tilt_at, roll),
  zoom_rotation?}` — `satellite` = dark NASA Blue Marble texture, teal ocean, thin light borders, flat
  fills (red #A83232, magenta #B0309A, blue-violet #5560B8, teal). Note **lat, lon order** here (geo
  layers use lon, lat).
- `map_pin {map?, lat, lon, label, tag_style: "box", side?, label_size?}` — city tag (white box, black
  caps).
- `map_route {map, from, to, label?: "11 MINS", label_at?: 0.5, follow_tangent?: true, line_style?:
  solid|dashed, arrow_head?: true, draw?}`.
- `route_follow {from, to (country or [lat, lon]), map?, style?, avatar?, arrow_head?, line_style?, draw?
  (2.2), vehicle?: cut-out (facing right), orient: true, vehicle_angle, vehicle_size, trail_fade?,
  land_highlight?: {fill, label} | false, from_highlight?, label?, label_at?, follow_tangent?, follow?
  (0.35), fill?, clouds?}` — white arc draws A → B, the map keeps the tip in frame, motion blur on.
- `map_fly {map?, from, to, style?, colors?: [from, to], clouds?}` — pan / zoom from A out to both and in
  to B, highlighting each.
- `needle_pin {map?, country | lat+lon, label, color}` · `avatar_pin {map?, country | lat+lon, media
  (face), label}`.
- `map_tilt {map?, tilt? (38), roll? (-10), at?, duration? (0.6), scale?}` — map pitches back (moves into
  precomp `<map>_tilt`, comp layer `<map>_tilted`; later map ops need `in_comp: "<map>_tilt"`).
- `terrain_label {map?, text ("ANDES"), along: [[lat, lon], …], size? (0.045), spread? (0.8), glyphs?:
  peaks|none, stagger?}` — letter-spaced label along a range / river.
- `map_watermark {map?, code, text?, size? (0.35 h), opacity? (60), rotate?: auto|deg}` — giant ghost
  country word.
- `status_ring {attach | lat+lon | x, y, size? (0.06), color? (#D0202A), dashed?, spin? (4 s), glow?}` ·
  `signal_rings {attach | lat+lon | x, y, color?, count? (3), period? (0.75), flatten? (0.35),
  max_radius? (0.12)}` (radio / signals — use on the NK radio) · `pulse_rings {…}` ("here", epicentre).
- `geo_label {text, at: [x,y] | lat+lon | attach, pointer?: hook|line|none, side?, length?, size? (0.04),
  animator? (typewriter)}` · `path_text {text, path_layer? | points, offset?, size?, spacing?, lift?,
  typing?, cps? (14)}` (e.g. "ESCAPE ROUTE" typed along a dashed line).
- `search_sweep {place, label, vehicle?, ground?, beam_size? (0.12), path?, snow?, duration? (4.5)}` ·
  `sketch_map {items: [{icon: mountain|camp|crash|x|river|dot, x, y, label, arrow?, at?}], compass?,
  directions: [{label, side, at, reveal?}], paper?, duration? (7)}` (parchment ink sketch — good for the
  parents' escape plan).
- Map grammar: reveals 0.1–0.3 s after the keyword (`at`); one new map element every 1–2.5 s; red only
  for rings / marks / danger.
- Old Mohitflix plates: `tool/map_plate.py` / `plates2.py` render Natural Earth 10 m plates with India's
  official boundary when a static plate is needed.

