## 9. Transitions, mood and character FX

### 9.1 The `transition` op

`transition {from: outgoing layer, to: incoming layer, type, duration? (s), at? (cut time, default =
to.start), sound?: true (matched whoosh / riser / impact with its PEAK on the cut) | false | "<sfx kind>" |
[kinds], snap_to_beat?: true (beat_tolerance 0.25 s, or beats: [s]), params?: {…}}` — one undo step. It
extends / trims the two layers so they overlap around the cut and adds eased keyframes, masks, effects
and helper layers (ids `tr_<to>_*`). Re-running it on the same pair replaces it. `list_transitions {}`
prints the catalog. All 36 types with "best for", default duration, sound and params: **Appendix A.3**.

Mohitflix preference order (from the reference study): **camera travels to the next element (no cut)**
> rack focus / `focus_pull` > `push_through` / `zoom_into_photo` > paper slide > `light_leak_wipe` /
double exposure (blend screen) > `paper_tear` / `shatter` / `ink_bleed` (rare) > `glitch_cut` (chapter
cards only). **Never `dip_to_black` / `cut_to_black` mid-story** (Mohit: no black screens).

Gotchas (see 16): transitions add a **constant `motion_blur 100`** to comp layers — keyframe it to 0
outside the transition window or remove it (it caused black / smeared frames). There is **no `flash`
transition type** — use `flash_cut` or `exposure_in`.

### 9.2 V3 documentary transitions (params)

`powder_burst {direction, kind: snow|dust|sand|ash, color, density 80, linger 0.3}` · `debris_burst {kind:
ice|snow|cloud|glass|dust|leaves, from: center|…|bottom_right, pre_roll 1.2, peak_cover 100, tail 0.5,
tone}` · `frost_shatter {corner}` · `zoom_blur {zoom 2.5, flash, grain, cx, cy}` (evidence →
reenactment) · `eye_reflection {point [x,y] pupil, size, opacity 70, linger 0.8}` · `holes {count 45,
size 10, rim}` · `shatter {tone: glass|ice|gold, lead_in 1.0, shard_color, cx, cy}` · `slice {bands 4,
stagger 30}` · `slant_wipe {direction, angle 10, edge 60}` · `shrink_to_card {size 0.45, bg, tilt -4,
hold 1.5, border}` · `emerge {target | point, from 0.05}` · `zoom_out_of_photo {layer | photo_box |
point+size}` · `slide_film {size 0.55, pink 30}` · `exposure_in {from 3.0, color}` · `punch_in` ·
`cut_to_black {silence: true}` · `ink_bleed {incoming: "duotone_of_outgoing"}`.

### 9.3 Mood and character FX (edit ops)

- `mood_flood {at, duration 0.9, hold 2.5, color "#E0283A", dark "#5A0A10", from: corner|side|center,
  keep: [ids in colour], sfx: braam|false}` — dread / despair (everything turns red mono from a corner).
- `tint_wipe {at, color "#D0101A", amount 70, from, duration 0.6, hold 2}`.
- `grade_swap {to: hope|warm|cold|dread|archive|normal, at, duration 0 (snap) | s, until?}` — **"Lekin
  woh galat hain" → snap to `cold`** with a punch-in and a bass hit.
- `spotlight_subject {keep: [ids], layers? | shot, others: {mono 100, dim 15, blur 0}, tint?, start,
  duration 3, attack 0.25, release 0.5}`.
- `pulse {layer, effect? tint | prop?, param?, from, to, period 1.0, start, duration 3, sync, sfx?:
  heartbeat}`.
- `lightning {at | [s, s+0.15], bolt, x 0.62, color, sfx: thunder}`.
- `montage {media: [ids], start, every 0.35, looks: [threshold, duotone_green, red_paint, magenta, grunge,
  crop], zoom 8, sound}` — one-breath recap.
- `swap_layer {layer, with: layer | media, at, transition: pop|cut|fade|flash, duration 0.2, sfx}` —
  in-place swap (day room → night room, empty frame → portrait).
- `set_dof {keys: [{t, focus}], aperture?}` — rack focus (5.3).
- `speech_bubble` (7.1), `animate_in` presets `punch_in`, `swing_in`, `exposure_in`.
- Effects used by these: `burst, radial_blur, holes, frost, cracks, threshold, red_paint, lightning,
  slices, slant_wipe, slide_mount, puff, burn_edge {progress, cx, cy, color, embers}, page_curl {progress,
  angle, shadow, back}`.

## 10. Sound: SFX, beds, music, beat sync, mix

All SFX are **synthesised on the device** — never ask for sound files for these. Real music / SFX files
(e.g. `Downloads\NK_EP01\music\*.mp3`, `sfx\*.wav`, `sfx_cc0\*.wav`) come in with `import_media` and an
`audio` layer.

- `add_sfx {kind, time? (the sound's PEAK lands here, e.g. on the cut), volume? (0-200, auto-levelled),
  duration? (beds loop to fill it, with fades), id?}`. Kinds:
  - transitions: `whoosh, swoosh_short, swoosh_long, swoosh_reverse` (sucks in, stops on the cut),
    `whoosh_silence` (builds then cuts to dead silence before a reveal), `reverse_cymbal, riser`;
  - impacts: `hit, impact` (slam decaying to silence), `braam, sub_drop`;
  - UI / text: `tick, pop, ui_click, ding, typewriter, glitch`;
  - foley: `shutter` (photo), `paper` (documents / articles), `pin_drop` (peak = landing), `heartbeat`,
    `marker` (handwriting), `radio_crackle`, `thunder`, `powder_whoosh`, `ice_crash`, `puff`;
  - loopable beds: `crowd_bed, wind_bed, room_tone, night_bed, rain_bed, fire_bed, clock_tick`.
- `add_sfx {mood: "rain|night|war|crowd|desert|suspense|office…", time, duration}` — ambience bed.
- `add_sfx {kind: "typewriter", layer: <text layer with animator typewriter>}` — one click per letter.
- `beat_sync {mode: "cuts", music?, tolerance? (0.25), layers?}` — moves every cut onto the nearest beat
  (SFX on cuts follow) · `{mode: "pops", layers?, downbeats?}` — text pops / cards start on beats ·
  `{mode: "drop", music, at, drop?, preroll?, fade_in?}` — re-cues the music so its drop hits at `at`.
  Beats come from the analysed music, else pass `bpm` (+ `offset`) or `beats: [s]`. (Windows: beat
  analysis of non-WAV music needs the ffmpeg PCM source; convert to WAV if analysis fails.)
- `auto_mix {roles?: {layerId: voice|music|sfx|ambience|none}, duck?: true, fades?: true, targets?:
  {voice: -16, music: -28, sfx: -20, ambience: -32}}` — loudness-normalises every audio track, ducks
  music under the voice, fades music / ambience in and out. **Run it last.**
- Volume automation: `set_keyframe {target: <audio layer>, prop: "volume", time, value}`.
- Good habits: whoosh / swoosh on every camera travel and transition, `pin_drop` on map pins, `paper` on
  articles, `shutter` on photo cards, `braam` / `sub_drop` under a big reveal, `whoosh_silence` before a
  shocking line, a mood bed under every scene (NK home: `room_tone` + `night_bed` at night + radio
  murmur), `auto_mix` at the end.

