## 13. Director, story patterns and automatic building

### 13.1 Director

`director_run` (3.8) plans a documentary storyboard from a brief / script and the project media and
builds the whole timeline (chapters hook / context / conflict / turning point / ending, pacing rules,
variety repair, B-roll moves, components, captions, SFX, music duck, frame review). It uses **MotionAI's
own AI connection** (AI tab: ChatGPT sign-in or API key). For Mohitflix premium work, Claude usually
builds by hand with `run_commands` for full control; the Director is good for rough cuts.

### 13.2 Story patterns (Nitish-Rajput grammar)

`suggest_patterns {lines, …}` (read-only) → a plan of beats `{pattern, role, start, end, reveal_at,
slots, transition_in, grade, overlays, sfx, events}` + `resolved` (what each pattern uses on this build) +
`stats` (asl, presenter_share, max_presenter_gap, same_pattern_repeats, max_element_gap). Build with
`run_commands [{"op":"apply_patterns","plan":…,"assets":{presenter: video id, broll: [ids], beats:
{"<i>": {media, places, quote, …}}},"tone":…,"sfx":true,"prefix":…}]`. `list_patterns {category?}` prints
the registry.

Grammar: a shot every ~3.4 s, a new element every 1–2.5 s; reveals 0.1–0.3 s after the keyword;
evidence (article / book / note) is ALWAYS followed by a reenactment; never the same pattern twice in a
row; presenter 25–30 % (Mohitflix cold opens have no presenter: pass `presenter: false`).

Pattern ids by trigger (category: ids):
- **maps:** satellite_country_map (country / city named), route_arrow_follow ("X se Y tak"),
  map_zoom_punch, map_tilt_3d (mountains, rivers, borders), giant_ghost_country, route_duration_label,
  signal_rings (radio calls), status_ring, geo_label, search_sweep, sketch_map (directions / plans),
  map_labels_typed.
- **evidence:** doc_highlight_circle (any source quoted), book_reveal_open, zoom_out_to_source,
  source_tag, grunge_photo_title, note_card (PLAN, RULE), photo_wall, handwrite_card, emblem_badge,
  montage, article_focus, circle_mark, inset_circle (an object mentioned — the radio), quote_hole,
  list_card, stain_doodle.
- **data:** unit_chart, people_grid_tally, stat_figure, comparison_split, gauge_hud, clock_stamp (exact
  time — "raat ka waqt"), stat_behind_silhouettes, ui_toggle, audio_wave_flag (broadcasts), calendar_flip,
  clock_overlay, stat_title.
- **overlay:** icon_sticker, icon_drop, kinetic_text.
- **presenter:** social_cta, presenter_stats, presenter_punch_in, social_bug, presenter.
- **character:** surface_labels (naming a person), speech_bubble_comic, swing_in, swap_layer, rack_focus,
  spotlight_subject, speech_bubble_puff, censor_bar (ALWAYS over AI likenesses of real people).
- **transition:** zoom_blur, debris_burst, slide_film, slice, slant_wipe, shrink_to_card, emerge,
  ink_bleed_duotone, eye_zoom_through, powder_burst, eye_reflection, holes, shatter_ice, push_through,
  foreground_wipe, map_drop, flash_cut, light_leak_wipe.
- **mood:** mood_flood, grade_swap, cut_to_black, lightning, pulse, sun_glare_entry, crash_to_black.
- **shot:** reenactment_shot, crane_down_reveal, push_between_subjects, rack_focus_encounter,
  fog_tracking, human_detail_insert.

