## 14. Looking at your work

- **Loop:** build → `batch [run_commands, check_scene, preview_shot]` → read the problems and the
  sheet → fix → look again. Apply `fix_all` only after reading it.
- `preview_shot {from, to, count: 8–12, format: "jpeg"}` for moves; `render_frame {time, width: 1920}`
  for one detail; `editor_screenshot` to confirm what Mohit sees in the editor.
- Watch for: black or empty frames (rule 0.1.8), edges of plates showing, floating cut-outs, text
  outside the safe area, a still frame longer than ~1 s (target ≤ 4 % still time), harsh pops.
- Side-by-side with references: render the key frames, put them next to the reference frames (Mohit's
  `C:\YT\Tools\Ref\All_Videos_No_Narrator` contact sheets) and judge honestly before sending.
- `render_frame` is slow with particles / light rays (~5–10 s per frame): use jpeg and fewer tiles.

## 15. Export

- `export_video {resolution: 1080, file_name: "NK_EP01_test.mp4", folder: "<abs path>", wait: false}` →
  job id; then `export_status {wait_s: 100}` until `done` (gives the output file) or `failed` (reason; also
  `get_logs {level: "error"}`).
- Exports the **main** comp. GPU encoders (NVENC on Mohit's RTX 4060 / QSV / AMF, else x264); 720p–4K;
  high_quality true by default. "Use high-performance GPU" button in the app if NVENC is not used.
- Don't edit, press keys in MotionAI, or minimise the window during an export. Cancel needs confirmation
  in the app (`cancel_job` asks it to stop).
- Deliver: tell Mohit the file path (default `Videos\MotionAI`), or stage it with the device tools and
  send it.

## 16. Known quirks and workarounds (verified in code, win-41)

| # | Quirk | Workaround |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `add_layer` applies only `position` and `scale` from the transform. **`anchor`, `rotation`, `opacity` and `blend` given at creation are ignored** (also on nulls and shapes) | `set_keyframe` anchor / rotation / opacity at the layer's start time; `update_layer {blend}` |
| 2 | `update_layer` has no transform fields: **scale / position / rotation / opacity there are ignored** | `set_property` (static) or `set_keyframe` |
| 3 | `"parent": ""` → error "Parent "" does not exist" | Omit `parent` when there is none; `update_layer {parent: null}` to un-parent |
| 4 | Images over 4096 px (long side) are downsized on import | Keep plates ≤ 4096 px and scale up with keyframes |
| 5 | The `transition` op adds a **constant `motion_blur` (amount 100, some types 60–70)** to the comp layers it touches; it caused black / smeared frames when layers moved | After `transition`, keyframe that layer's `motion_blur` amount to 0 outside the transition window (or `remove_effect`) |
| 6 | There is no transition type `flash` (error) | `flash_cut`, `exposure_in`, or `animate_in {preset: "flash"}` |
| 7 | `add_shot` frames exteriors well; interiors via `add_shot` / `make_3d + camera_shot` framed badly | Rooms: `room` component (5.7) or the manual parallax rig (5.5) |
| 8 | `update_shot` refuses when the shot comp is used elsewhere | Duplicate / rebuild the shot, or remove the other use first |
| 9 | Tall page images (e.g. 1600×2000) did not render | Use landscape pages (1920×1300) |
| 10 | `blur` on a 3D layer is broken; `scramble` on Devanagari is broken (`check_scene` flags both) | DOF (`set_dof`) for 3D; another animator for Hindi |
| 11 | While the MotionAI window is **minimised**, Windows draws nothing: `render_frame` / export fail, and `new_project` / `open_project` time out with "The editor did not open" (the project is still created / saved) | Ask Mohit to restore the window, then `open_project {id}` |
| 12 | Commands without `start` / `time` used to use the playhead (V1); V2-B defaults `start` to 0 | Always pass explicit times |
| 13 | `blend` together with a track matte on one layer is not supported | Put the matte on a precomp, or drop the blend |
| 14 | `render_frame` with particles / light rays is slow (5–10 s) | jpeg, fewer frames, `preview_shot` |
| 15 | Browser-pane sessions lose `window.*` helpers on reload; another tab can become active | Re-install helpers; always pass `tabId` |
| 16 | Beat analysis of mp3 / m4a on Windows may be unavailable (PCM source) | Provide WAV music, or pass `bpm` / `beats` to `beat_sync` |
| 17 | Some features may read `project.main` instead of the open precomp | Prefer `in_comp` and check results with `preview_shot {comp}` |

If you hit a new quirk, add it here (section 20) with the verified workaround.

