## 18. Quality checklist (the reference style)

From the study of 34 reference videos (785 narrator-free clips):

- **Something always moves.** Only 3.9 % of time is still (0 % in 2025 videos): target ≤ 4 %. Few hard
  cuts; shots often 15–50 s with the camera travelling element to element. A **new detail every 1.5–3 s**.
- **2025 style:** photoreal AI recreations of story moments + paper evidence laid over the moving scene
  (article cards, source notes, name tags, CCTV time stamps); light-grey relief maps with saturated country
  fills and HUGE 3D country names.
- **Article card:** cream crumpled paper; left text block ~55 % width: red date pill → bold serif headline
  → 3–6 body lines → wordmark bottom-left; yellow highlighter wipes the exact phrase as it is spoken; red
  pen circle on one word; B&W cut-out of the subject bleeding off the bottom-right; slow push 3–6 s.
- **Narration → visual:** imagine → slow push into an AI POV scene; place → map fly-in then the location
  + red location pill; date → timeline ruler pill or giant year; sourced fact → article card highlighting
  the spoken phrase; new person → cut-out + name plate (later a circle badge); listed items → each item lit
  / labelled on its word; number → big counter; contrast → split + crack; rule / law → document + stamp;
  negation → option appears then red strike; twist → snap push-in + bass hit + colder grade; question →
  big white words on dark; time passes → relight the same set + time stamp.
- **Look:** warm amber / teal-orange grade, film grain, soft vignette, shallow DOF, dust in light beams,
  subtle lens breathing; maps clean and bright.
- **Layers, not flat cut-outs:** every scene has bg / mid / fg with different motion; cut-outs get
  `match_colour`, contact shadows, light wrap; foreground objects pass the lens.
- **Sound:** music bed + room tone always; a whoosh on every travel; paper / marker / tick foley on cards
  and labels; braam / sub drop on reveals; `auto_mix` last.
- **Never:** black screens mid-story, hard cuts to black, long text blocks, real logos, reused creator
  footage, maps of India without the official boundary.
- Before sending: `check_scene` clean, `preview_shot` of every shot, frames side by side with the
  references, honest verdict.

